{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For the tree was good for food</b> — she had assumed that it was bitter and a deadly poison, and that therefore He warned us against it. But now she saw that it was good and sweet to eat." "<b>And that it was a desire to the eyes</b> — through it one desires and pursues what his eyes see." "<b>And the tree was desirable to make one wise</b> — for through it one becomes wise to desire, and desire is given to the eyes while desirability is in the intellect. The upshot is that through it one wills and chooses a thing or its opposite."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:05.586942441Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}